` "A guard of the wrong polarity protects nothing: or's second argument runs when x is not a block, and so does and's after a negated test. Both calls warn (eu-oaz72.194)."
h-or(x): or(x block?, x.a)

` "and after a negated block? test."
h-and-not(x): and(x block? not, x.a)

bad-or: h-or(3)
bad-and-not: h-and-not(3)
